## Parser Testing Strategy

Data parsers require specialized testing approaches due to their critical role in data integrity and the variety of input formats they must handle.

### Testing Layers for Parsers

**Unit Tests** (`*.test.ts`):
- Test individual parsing functions with controlled inputs
- Validate error handling for malformed data
- Check edge cases (empty files, special characters, encoding issues)
- Verify field mapping and type conversions

**Integration Tests** (`*.integration.test.ts`):
- Test with real-world export files from actual services
- Validate end-to-end parsing of complete datasets
- Ensure preservation of original data without unwanted transformations
- Test parser performance with large files

### Data Preservation Philosophy

Parsers should **preserve original data** rather than perform intelligent transformations:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Preserve original data
const result = {
  item_type: getValue('category') || 'Other', // Use exactly what's provided
  brand: getValue('brand') || null,           // Don't guess from descriptions
  description: getValue('name'),              // Map fields directly
  weight_unit_display: unit                   // Keep original units
}

// ❌ BAD: Intelligent transformations
const result = {
  item_type: detectCategory(description),     // Don't auto-categorize
  brand: extractBrandFromText(description),   // Don't guess brands
  description: cleanupText(getValue('name'))  // Don't modify text
}
```

### Integration Test Pattern

```typescript
describe('Real-world CSV parsing', () => {
  it('should parse actual LighterPack export', () => {
    const csvContent = readFileSync('examples/lighterpack-export.csv', 'utf-8')
    const result = parseCsv(csvContent)

    expect(result.success).toBe(true)
    expect(result.data.length).toBeGreaterThan(10)

    // Test specific items without making assumptions about transformations
    const tent = result.data.find(item => item.description === 'Tent')
    expect(tent?.weight_g).toBeGreaterThan(0)
    expect(tent?.item_type).toBeDefined() // Don't assume specific category
  })
})
```

